  "ddc": {
    "url": "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1WaxvbLx7UoSZaBqdFr1u32F2uWVLo-CJunJB4nlGUE4/htmlview/sheet?gid=1662574278",
    "row": 113,
    "htmlId": "1662574278R112",
    "text": "   113   Headseeker        Upon dealing direct   non-Precision Weapon Damage  :  Grants  increased Precision Damage  and 3?% Increased Auto Aim Cone Size for 0.55 seconds.   Dealing additional   Non-Precision Damage   refreshes the buff duration.   The perk actually multiplies the   Precision Bonus   by 1.2x, but the actual   Precision Damage Increase   results are easier to explain.      Precision Damage Increase  per Intrinsic Frame: Adaptive Pulse =  7.1%  | Aggressive Pulse =  10%  | Heavy Burst Pulse =  9.5%  High-Impact Pulse =  8.74%  | Lightweight Pulse =  6.3%  | Rapid-Fire Pulse =  10.3%  Adaptive Burst Sidearm =  8.46%  | Heavy Burst Sidearm =  7.36%  Precision Scout Rifle =  8.66%  Heavy Burst Hand Cannon =  7% increased Weakspot Damage.    ↑Passively grants +5 Stability.    What even is a   Weakspot  ? How is it different from a   Precision Hit  ?   Weakspot Hits   that do not register as a   Precision Hit   can still benefit or trigger   Weakspot   effects, such as Headseeker, or Heavy Burst Hand Cannon's intrinsic 9.5% Weakspot Damage Buff. Similarly,   Precision Hits   are not always scored on   Weakspots  , and may not trigger   Weakspot effects  . One such example are   Shielded Combatants  .   Weakspot Damage Increases   will work when other   Precision Hit Increases     wouldn't  .   ",
    "html": "<tr style=\"height: 254px\"><th id=\"1662574278R112\" style=\"height: 254px;\"><div style=\"line-height: 254px\">113</div></th><td class=\"s48\">Headseeker</td><td class=\"s26\"><div style=\"width:70px;height:254px;\"><img src=\"https://docs.google.com/sheets-images-rt/AO43MLYFdTZHysSpyUdNER8Nfv5rm-bztpDfhAyLfRtUTP2lSr_ERaZdwzrkZe3JhLccZ9R_uRS98AU0-LRJ0fLEPiNdaEhlwAXOnYKjh035dioHyZ_xrZTeelj-OdJP4K0JHfq4JyN1mVlVSRA8ps4E-tcnuFt3lT59LCLP=w70-h254\" style=\"width:inherit;height:inherit;object-fit:scale-down;object-position:center center;pointer-events:none;\"/></div></td><td class=\"s16\" colspan=\"4\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\">Upon dealing direct </span><span style=\"font-style:italic;color:#999999;\">non-Precision Weapon Damage</span><span style=\"font-style:italic;\">:<br></span>Grants <span style=\"color:#f1c232;\">increased Precision Damage </span>and 3?% Increased Auto Aim Cone Size for 0.55 seconds. <br><span style=\"font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\">Dealing additional </span><span style=\"font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;color:#999999;\">Non-Precision Damage</span><span style=\"font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\"> refreshes the buff duration.<br></span><span style=\"font-size:6pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\">The perk actually multiplies the </span><span style=\"font-size:6pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;color:#f1c232;\">Precision Bonus</span><span style=\"font-size:6pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\"> by 1.2x, but the actual </span><span style=\"font-size:6pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;color:#f1c232;\">Precision Damage Increase </span><span style=\"font-size:6pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\">results are easier to explain.<br></span><span style=\"font-size:7pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#f1c232;\">Precision Damage Increase</span> per Intrinsic Frame:<br>Adaptive Pulse = <span style=\"color:#f1c232;\">7.1%</span> | Aggressive Pulse = <span style=\"color:#f1c232;\">10% </span>| Heavy Burst Pulse = <span style=\"color:#f1c232;\">9.5%</span><br>High-Impact Pulse = <span style=\"color:#f1c232;\">8.74%</span> | Lightweight Pulse = <span style=\"color:#f1c232;\">6.3% </span>| Rapid-Fire Pulse = <span style=\"color:#f1c232;\">10.3%</span><br>Adaptive Burst Sidearm = <span style=\"color:#f1c232;\">8.46% </span>| Heavy Burst Sidearm = <span style=\"color:#ffd966;\">7.36%</span><br>Precision Scout Rifle = <span style=\"color:#ffd966;\">8.66%<br></span>Heavy Burst Hand Cannon =<span style=\"color:#e69138;\"> 7% increased Weakspot Damage.<br></span><br><span style=\"color:#ffd966;\">↑Passively grants +5 Stability.<br><br></span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;\">What even is a </span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;color:#e69138;\">Weakspot</span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;\">? How is it different from a </span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;color:#ffd966;\">Precision Hit</span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;\">?<br></span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;color:#e69138;\">Weakspot Hits</span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\"> that do not register as a </span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;color:#f1c232;\">Precision Hit</span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\"> can still benefit or trigger </span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;color:#e69138;\">Weakspot</span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\"> effects, such as Headseeker, or Heavy Burst Hand Cannon&#39;s intrinsic 9.5% Weakspot Damage Buff.<br>Similarly, </span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;color:#f1c232;\">Precision Hits</span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\"> are not always scored on </span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;color:#e69138;\">Weakspots</span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\">, and may not trigger </span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;color:#e69138;\">Weakspot effects</span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\">.<br>One such example are </span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;color:#a4c2f4;\">Shielded Combatants</span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\">. </span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;color:#e69138;\">Weakspot Damage Increases</span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\"> will work when other </span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;color:#f1c232;\">Precision Hit Increases</span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-style:italic;color:#e06666;\">wouldn&#39;t</span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic;\">.</span></td></tr>"
  },
  "formula": "totalPrecision + (totalPrecision - totalPrecision / baseCritMultiplier) * 0.2",
  "limitations": [
    "Uncertain 3?% Auto Aim Cone Size is unimplemented; no aim assistance is invented.",
    "Enhanced passive +5 Stability is excluded; only base hash 460017080 is supported.",
    "The port exposes a precision boolean. Original weakspot versus precision-hit and shielded-combatant distinctions are not modeled; this is not full Destiny weakspot parity.",
    "Uses the existing source-entry WeaponBallistics precision multiplier, not the DDC per-frame total-damage percentages.",
    "Only positive actual direct-hit weapon loss activates/refreshes. No splash, ability, blocked/immune hit, preview or unpaid emission credit.",
    "11 ticks is 0.55 seconds at 20 TPS. Accepted stow clears the window; paid emission snapshots cannot gain a buff from their own nonprecision hit."
  ]
}
